# A/B: two more duplicated copies removed (depth-0 qcoeff raster, DPB refresh)

date: 2026-08-13
host: mac (Apple aarch64, 12 logical cores; box idle, top foreign 5.9% CPU)
base: 6ad044d00   cand: this commit
harness: rust/tools/perf_ab.sh, interleaved paired, randomised per-round order,
         NEITHER SIDE NICED, both arms `-C llvm-args=-align-all-functions=4`.
grid:    content=gradient sizes=[256 512 1024] presets=[6 10] qp=40 rounds=21
ident:   all cells ident=Y; byteid_fingerprint 168/168 unchanged AND == C;
         decode_gate_grid 120/120; partial_sb_gate 146/146; recon_parity
         432/432; workspace nextest 1029/1029.

| size | preset | n  | cand ratio | control ratio | cand-vs-control |
|-----:|:------:|---:|-----------:|--------------:|----------------:|
|  256 | 6      | 21 |     1.0043 |        0.9956 |          +0.9pp |
|  256 | 10     | 21 |     0.9782 |        1.0099 |          −3.2pp |
|  512 | 6      | 21 |     1.0024 |        0.9937 |          +0.9pp |
|  512 | 10     | 21 |     0.9782 |        0.9980 |          −2.0pp |
| 1024 | 6      | 21 |     0.9966 |        0.9971 |          −0.1pp |
| 1024 | 10     | 21 |     0.9883 |        0.9987 |          −1.0pp |

Control = the base binary against a byte-identical copy of itself, run in the
same session. Reads ~1-2% at p10, null at p6 — the same tier split as the two
earlier decision-path changes, for the same reason (p6 spends far longer per
block inside the RD search itself).

## What the two changes remove

1. **`funnel_block_decision`'s depth-0 qcoeff "unpack".** At `tx_depth == 0` it
   allocated a fresh `w*h` `i32` raster and copied the packed txb into its
   `min(w,32) x min(h,32)` corner. On every block WITHOUT a 64-dim side —
   i.e. `pw == w && ph == h` — that is a byte-for-byte copy of a buffer that
   is dropped two lines later, so it is now a `mem::take`. Blocks with a
   64-wide or 64-tall transform still unpack, because there the raster really
   is larger than the packed corner and the rows/columns past 32 must be zero.

2. **`DecodedPictureBuffer::refresh` cloned the whole picture once per set
   bit.** A KEY frame's `refresh_frame_flags` is 0xFF, so a single still-image
   encode deep-cloned its Y plane EIGHT times into eight slots that are only
   ever read through `&ReferenceFrame`. The slots now hold
   `Arc<ReferenceFrame>` and `refresh` clones once. Private field; `store`,
   `get` and `refresh` keep their signatures, so no API change.

Profile that pointed at (2): `DecodedPictureBuffer::refresh` was 4.2% of the
`libsystem_platform` (memmove/memset/bzero) self samples at gradient 512x512
preset 10.
